1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,533
As data goes down the stack at the sender, each layer wraps it in its own header.

2
00:00:05,533 --> 00:00:08,867
Transport adds port numbers to make a segment.

3
00:00:08,867 --> 00:00:12,513
Network adds IP addresses to make a packet.

4
00:00:12,513 --> 00:00:16,953
Data link adds MAC addresses and a checksum to make a frame.

5
00:00:16,953 --> 00:00:19,661
The physical layer sends it as bits.

6
00:00:19,661 --> 00:00:23,815
At the receiver, each layer strips its header off on the way up.

7
00:00:23,815 --> 00:00:26,315
This wrapping is called encapsulation.

